@id: scene.057_enforced_enrollment
@when: Unknown.scene_057_enforced_enrollment
@where: Realm/Physical/Unknown
@scope: narrative
@entities: [Geralt, Kyh]

=segments:
  - line: 1
    type: narration
    text: "Chapter 55 the man behind the armor"
  - line: 3
    type: narration
    text: "The Guild's wards hummed as Geralt crossed the threshold—not a barrier, but a sieve, testing the harmonics of his borrowed divinity."
  - line: 4
    type: narration
    text: "Behind him, Oreck's tail lashed once against the lunar dust before the reptilian warrior melted into the sprawl's shadows."
  - line: 5
    type: narration
    text: "Inside, the air smelled of ozone and something deeper, like the scent of an old blade being reforged."
  - line: 7
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh moved too smoothly beside him, her shadow-form rippling with unnatural precision."
  - line: 8
    type: narration
    text: "When the hematite-eyed archivist revealed the hololith of the breeding pits—rows upon rows of dragon eggs suspended in silvered amniotic fluid, each pulsing with the same rhythm as the net that took Vaelthane—her fingers twitched toward the projection."
  - line: 9
    type: narration
    text: "\"The promised land,\" she murmured, so softly only Geralt's enhanced hearing caught it."
  - line: 10
    type: narration
    text: "By the time Luminaire turned to look, her face was blank again, edges perfectly composed."
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "The Applicator in Geralt's spine burned as he slammed his palm against the enrollment plinth."
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "\"Finish it.\" The Guild's representatives recoiled as the third ring—the nameless one—darkened to the color of a starless sky."
  - line: 14
    type: narration
    text: "Some foundations had to be forced."
  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "The network's acceptance flared through him, a thousand synaptic connections snapping into place with the finality of a vault door sealing."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "Around them, the guild's ancient stones trembled, whispering of debts now called due."
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "Outside, unseen by any in the sanctum, Earth's last patch of blue winked out beneath the Queen's porcelain hand."
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow deepened in the corners where no light reached."
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "The plinth's fractured shards still hung suspended in the air when Geralt stepped forward, his shadow stretching long and jagged across the guild's sanctum."
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's fingers brushed his wrist—a silent plea for restraint—but he shook her off with a twitch of muscle beneath the Dragon Mail."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "The twelve sovereigns watched from their elevated benches, their faces carefully neutral, their hands folded in identical postures of condescension."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "Documentation."
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "Always documentation."
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "As if history could be contained in ink and vellum."
  - line: 29
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Geralt
    text: "\"You've recorded storms,\""
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "The hematite-eyed archivist inhaled sharply."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "Names had weight here."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "True names especially."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "The Dragon Mail's pauldrons hissed as they unfolded, revealing the latticework of old wounds beneath—not just battle scars, but the precise, surgical marks of a man who'd been taken apart and reassembled too many times."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "\"Ragnarok's Shadow,\" Geralt continued, tapping one jagged line along his collarbone."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "\"Breaker of Chains,\" he added, tracing the brand on his forearm."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "Each title was a scar, each scar a story they'd documented but never *witnessed*."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "He let his hand drop."
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "\"You've written about anchors."
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "Have you ever held one?\""
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "Then, from the highest bench, a dry chuckle."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "The eldest sovereign—a being with too many jointed fingers—leaned forward."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "\"We know what you are, Geralt of No House."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "A spliced soul."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "A living contradiction.\""
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt smiled."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "It wasn't pleasant."
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "\"Then you know this.\" He slammed his fist into the plinth's wreckage."
  - line: 53
    type: narration
    text: "The third ring's fragments *sang*, their pitch rising until the guild's ancient stones vibrated like struck glass."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "The sound wasn't just noise—it was a frequency, the same harmonic that had thrummed through Vaelthane's wings before the net took him."
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow flared black in the sudden resonance."
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "The sovereigns clutched their ears."
  - line: 58
    type: narration
    text: "Only Geralt stood unmoved, his scars glowing faintly under the strain."
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "\"You want enrollment?\" he shouted over the din."
  - line: 60
    type: narration
    text: "\"Then hear the *sound* of your documentation burning.\""
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "The ringing silence after the third ring's shattering was its own kind of violence."
  - line: 63
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt watched the guild's sovereigns—twelve faces carved from various species' ideals of wisdom—blink in staggered unison, their pupils dilating against the afterimage of harmonic disruption."
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "One, a Threnody singer whose throat-sacs pulsed with muted distress, reached instinctively for the ledger at her bench."
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "Her fingers passed through it as though it were mist."
  - line: 66
    type: narration
    text: "Ink-stained documentation didn't just dissolve; it *unwrote itself*, lines of text retreating into the vellum like startled eels."
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh exhaled through her teeth—a sound like a blade leaving its sheath."
  - line: 69
    type: narration
    text: "\"You broke their records,\" she murmured."
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "The guild's archive walls, usually alive with softly glowing sigils, now stood dark."
  - line: 72
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt flexed his hand, watching silvered scars ripple."
  - line: 73
    type: narration
    text: "\"No."
  - line: 74
    type: narration
    text: "I broke the *narrative*.\""
  - line: 76
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla, hunched near the sanctum's entrance, made a wet sound of approval."
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "His clay fingers kneaded the guild's threshold stone like dough."
  - line: 78
    type: narration
    text: "\"Bad mortar,\" he muttered."
  - line: 79
    type: narration
    text: "\"Cracks where they painted over them.\""
  - line: 81
    type: narration
    text: "The eldest sovereign recovered first."
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "Too many-jointed fingers steepled under a chin that wasn't there a moment ago."
  - line: 83
    type: narration
    text: "\"The third ring was never meant to be struck,\" it said, voice like a glacier calving."
  - line: 84
    type: narration
    text: "\"Its resonance is *structural*.\""
  - line: 86
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn't grace that with an answer."
  - line: 87
    type: narration
    text: "He turned instead toward the guild's great oculus, where Earth hung like a gutted jewel."
  - line: 88
    type: narration
    text: "The last blue was gone now, swallowed by the Queen's relentless white."
  - line: 89
    type: narration
    text: "But something new flickered at the edges—a tremble in the monochrome, subtle as a heartbeat under skin."
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh saw it too."
  - line: 92
    type: narration
    text: "Her shadow elongated toward the oculus, drawn like a compass needle."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "\"The dragons,\" she breathed."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "\"They're singing back.\""
  - line: 96
    type: narration
    text: "The hematite-eyed archivist made a small, devastated sound."
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt knew why."
  - line: 98
    type: narration
    text: "The observatory's lenses were aligned with Dragonwayne's ecliptic plane."
  - line: 99
    type: narration
    text: "Not a slaughterhouse."
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "A *resonance chamber*."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "Outside, the lunar sky shuddered."
  - line: 103
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere in the dark, Vaelthane's absence was a wound the cosmos couldn't stitch."
  - line: 105
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt rolled his shoulders, feeling the Dragon Mail's failing enchantments bite into flesh."
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "The guild's enrollment lay in ruins at his feet."
  - line: 107
    type: narration
    text: "The third ring's fragments still hummed against the stone, their pitch deepening."
  - line: 109
    type: narration
    text: "He stepped over them."
  - line: 111
    type: narration
    text: "The guild's silence was heavier than the moon's gravity—deliberate, pressurized, the quiet of archivists recalculating reality's ledger."
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "Sovereigns exchanged glances through the floating debris of their shattered documentation, fingers twitching toward absent pens."
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "The hematite-eyed archivist moved first, stepping over the ruined plinth with the caution of a scholar navigating a battlefield."
  - line: 114
    type: narration
    text: "Their hands hovered above the third ring's fragments, not touching, merely measuring the resonance still humming through the sanctum's stones."
  - line: 115
    type: narration
    text: "\"A structural breach,\" they murmured."
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "\"Not in our records, but in the record-keeping itself.\""
  - line: 118
    type: narration
    text: "The hematite-eyed archivist’s fingers trembled as they traced the air above the third ring’s shards."
  - line: 119
    type: narration
    text: "\"You've destabilized more than our archives,\" they said, voice cracking under the weight of revelation."
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Queen’s frequency—it’s not just rewriting Earth."
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "It’s eroding the *substrate*.\""
  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt inhaled the scent of fractured ink and ozone—the guild's dying breath of neutrality."
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "The moment stretched, elastic."
  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "This was the demand coiled in his throat, the one Vaelthane was captured to make space for."
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "He stepped forward, his boots crushing vellum underfoot like fallen leaves."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "\"Your archives are already burning,\" he said, voice rough with harmonic backlash."
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "\"But ash makes good mortar.\""
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "The eldest sovereign's too-many fingers spasmed."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "\"You ask for integration into the Lunar Guild's core network?\" Its voice wavered between disbelief and something darker—the sound of a bridge realizing it's about to become a battleground."
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla chuckled wetly from the doorway, patting the threshold stone with approval."
  - line: 134
    type: narration
    text: "\"Bad joins need recasting.\" His clay fingers left lunar dust in the sovereign's hesitation cracks."
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt reached into the scorched ruin of his Applicator and withdrew a single glyph—not words, but the shape of a wound."
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "The guild's oculus darkened as he pressed it against the nearest archive wall."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "The stone didn't just accept it; the masonry *remembered* the mark, grooves aligning like old friends reuniting."
  - line: 139
    type: narration
    text: "\"You're already part of Earth's bones,\" he said."
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "\"You just forgot how to bend.\""
  - line: 142
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow split into fractals as the guild's wards finally recognized what they faced—not a petitioner, but a cornerstone."
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "The hematite-eyed archivist made a small, wounded noise as their quill snapped mid-sentence."
  - line: 145
    type: narration
    text: "Outside, the lunar sky trembled."
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's glyph pulsed once—a heartbeat in stone—and the guild's ancient foundations groaned awake."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's fingers lingered on the glyph-carved wall, its pulse syncing with the slow, subterranean groan of the guild's awakening foundations."
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "\"Is it done?\" His voice wasn't a question—it was the scrape of a blade being sheathed."
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "The hematite-eyed archivist didn't answer with words."
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "They lifted their hands, palms upturned, and let the disintegrating vellum of their leders sift through their fingers like black snow."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "Documentation reduced to dust."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "The eldest sovereign exhaled—a sound like a vault door sealing—and inclined its head once."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt turned toward the sanctum's arched exit, his Dragon Mail whispering against stone."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "Three paces from the threshold, he stopped."
  - line: 159
    type: narration
    text: "Not a hesitation, but a punctuation."
  - line: 160
    type: narration
    text: "\"Not now,\" he said, without looking back."
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "The guild's oculus reflected in his peripheral vision—Earth's white corpse hanging in the void."
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "\"Not tomorrow.\" Kulla's clay fingers paused mid-kneading, sensing the shift in tone."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "\"But someday,\" Geralt continued, \"Earth will call for you.\" His shadow stretched long across the sanctum floor, jagged where it intersected with Kyh's pooled darkness."
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "\"Not by my voice."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "By my doing.\""
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "Behind him, the hematite archivist's breath hitched."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "They understood."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "The third ring's shards still hummed against the floor, their resonance digging deeper than the guild's stone—deep enough to reach whatever remained of Earth's molten core."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stepped over the threshold."
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "His final words weren't prophecy; they were tectonic plates shifting."
  - line: 173
    type: narration
    text: "\"That sky will break."
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "That choreography of slaves and gods will shatter.\" The Dragon Mail's pauldrons locked into place with a sound like bones settling."
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "\"And when Earth takes its rightful place in the dark?\" A faint, feral smile touched his lips."
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "\"That started here."
  - line: 177
    type: narration
    text: "Today.\""
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow surged forward to follow him—then recoiled as the guild's wards flared crimson in her path."
  - line: 180
    type: narration
    text: "She hissed, spectral fingers curling into claws."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn't turn to see."
  - line: 182
    type: narration
    text: "He walked into the lunar sprawl's neon-drenched arteries alone, the guild's foundations still vibrating in his wake."
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "Outside, the false sky trembled."
  - line: 185
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere in the Dragonwayne Nebula, Vaelthane's absence was a dissonance the cosmos couldn't ignore."
  - line: 187
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn't walk to the lunar surface—he *thought* it into being beneath his boots, the regolith rearranging itself like a dreamer shifting blankets."
  - line: 188
    type: narration
    text: "The Guild's network thrummed in his marrow now, its pathways obeying the weight of his intention before his neurons finished firing."
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "He exhaled, and the sprawl's neon arteries dimmed behind him."
  - line: 190
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere in the underbelly markets, Oreck would be tasting copper on his tongue, feeling the pull like a fishhook in his ribs."
  - line: 192
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian warrior emerged from between two leaning hab-units before Geralt finished blinking."
  - line: 193
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's nostrils flared, his clawed hands flexing at the sudden translocation."
  - line: 194
    type: narration
    text: "No portal."
  - line: 195
    type: narration
    text: "No spell-circle."
  - line: 196
    type: narration
    text: "Just Geralt's certainty hardening into fact."
  - line: 197
    type: narration
    text: "\"You,\" Oreck growled, \"are getting heavy to ignore.\" His tail lashed once, stirring moondust into lazy spirals."
  - line: 199
    type: narration
    text: "The Guild's lobby doors parted before them without hinges moving—an architectural sigh."
  - line: 200
    type: narration
    text: "Inside, Kyh waited by the humming enrollment plinth, her shadow-form now stitched with silver threads where the network had claimed her."
  - line: 201
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla crouched beside her, patting the floor like a nervous mason."
  - line: 202
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn't speak."
  - line: 203
    type: narration
    text: "He thought *forward*, and the lobby's stonework unraveled around them in a slow-motion landslide of impossible geometry."
  - line: 205
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's claws sank into suddenly-greasy air as lunar light dissolved into something thicker—damp, loamy, singing with forgotten chlorophyll."
  - line: 206
    type: narration
    text: "The transition wasn't violent."
  - line: 207
    type: narration
    text: "It was inevitable."
  - line: 208
    type: narration
    text: "One heartbeat they stood on polished moonstone; the next, their boots sank into black earth veined with bioluminescent fungi."
  - line: 209
    type: narration
    text: "The Guild's spires rose around them unchanged, but the sky beyond its arched windows was no longer void."
  - line: 210
    type: narration
    text: "It pulsed white, yes—but now threaded through with the faintest cracks of cobalt, like ceramic under stress."
  - line: 212
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla sniffed the air, his clay face splitting into a grin."
  - line: 213
    type: narration
    text: "\"Better mortar,\" he announced, pressing a palm against the nearest wall."
  - line: 214
    type: narration
    text: "The stones sighed in response."
  - line: 215
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's silver-threaded shadow stretched toward the windows, her voice hushed."
  - line: 216
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Guild always was Earth's bones."
  - line: 217
    type: narration
    text: "We just forgot it could *move*.\""
  - line: 219
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt flexed his fingers, watching the network's light ripple beneath his skin."
  - line: 220
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in his chest remained—but now, it had roots."
  - line: 222
    type: narration
    text: "The loam clung to Geralt's boots like a memory refusing to fade—each step pulling threads of luminous mycelium into the air, delicate as smoke signals."
  - line: 223
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck crouched low, claws sifting through the black soil until they scraped something that hummed."
  - line: 224
    type: narration
    text: "\"Here,\" he growled, and the earth itself seemed to lean in, listening."
  - line: 225
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow-fingers traced invisible ley lines while Kulla pressed his clay palm flat against the ground, muttering about \"poor foundations\" even as the bioluminescent veins brightened under his touch."
  - line: 227
    type: narration
    text: "The first white bolt came without thunder—a silent incision across the sky that left the air smelling of burnt ozone and something older, like libraries burning."
  - line: 229
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla worked differently."
  - line: 230
    type: narration
    text: "He didn't carve—he rebuilt."
  - line: 231
    type: narration
    text: "Clay fingers scooped handfuls of luminous fungi, kneading them into the soil like a baker folding raisins into dough."
  - line: 232
    type: narration
    text: "Where his palms pressed, the earth gained density, its resonance shifting from organic murmur to architectural hum."
  - line: 233
    type: narration
    text: "\"Good bones,\" he grunted, patting a newly solidified patch."
  - line: 234
    type: narration
    text: "\"Bad acoustics.\" Oreck's answering snort sent a spray of bioluminescent spores swirling into the air."
  - line: 236
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt watched the spores catch in the false sky's cracks—tiny motes of defiance lodged in the Queen's porcelain perfection."
  - line: 237
    type: narration
    text: "He crouched, pressing his bare palm against the cool mycelial threads."
  - line: 238
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in his chest didn't fade, but the network recognized it anyway—not as absence, but as a different kind of fullness."
  - line: 239
    type: narration
    text: "The Applicator's scorched core flared once, etching their coordinates into the Guild's substrate with the permanence of a glacier's advance."
  - line: 241
    type: narration
    text: "A sound like settling bookbones rippled through the camp as the last anchor point locked into place."
  - line: 242
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's silver-threaded shadow stretched taut between the markers, forming a perimeter only those with Dragon Mail could perceive."
  - line: 243
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck tested it with an extended claw—the air resisted like thick honey before yielding."
  - line: 244
    type: narration
    text: "\"Heavy,\" he observed, licking the residue from his talons."
  - line: 245
    type: narration
    text: "\"Tastes like...\""
  - line: 247
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Home,\""
  - line: 248
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla finished, though none of them had ever seen this version of Earth before. The clay golem's grin split wider as the ground beneath them thrummed—not in pain, but in recognition. Some foundations insisted on being remembered."
  - line: 250
    type: narration
    text: "The white sky trembled again."
  - line: 251
    type: narration
    text: "White lightening strike every 47 minutes.. on time, Everytime."
  - line: 253
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt exhaled through his nose—not a sigh, but the controlled release of a man balancing tectonic plates."
  - line: 254
    type: narration
    text: "\"We find Zypher.\" The words hung between them, blunt as a dropped anvil."
  - line: 255
    type: narration
    text: "Not a plan."
  - line: 256
    type: narration
    text: "A compass needle dipped in blood."
  - line: 257
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere beyond the false sky, Vaelthane's absence yawned like an open grave."
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's laughter cut through the silence—a fractured, wet sound that didn't match her silver-stitched shadow."
  - line: 260
    type: narration
    text: "Her fingers traced glyphs in the air only she could see."
  - line: 261
    type: narration
    text: "\"The windless paths,\" she murmured to no one, then startled when Geralt's gauntlet landed on her shoulder."
  - line: 262
    type: narration
    text: "The contact made her edges ripple like disturbed ink."
  - line: 264
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Still with us?\""
  - line: 265
    type: narration
    text: "His voice was flint striking bone."
  - line: 267
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Of course,\""
  - line: 269
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn't ask the golem."
  - line: 270
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla paused mid-motion, regolith dripping between his fingers."
  - line: 271
    type: narration
    text: "\"Foundation holds,\" he grunted, patting the earth like a loyal hound."
  - line: 272
    type: narration
    text: "The ground pulsed once in agreement."
  - line: 274
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's claws flexed—a tell Geralt had learned decades ago on the blood-slick decks of Orion slave barges."
  - line: 275
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian warrior stared at the horizon where Earth's corpse hung wrapped in white frequency."
  - line: 276
    type: narration
    text: "His nostrils flared, tasting copper and ionized air."
  - line: 277
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt waited."
  - line: 278
    type: narration
    text: "Some choices couldn't be rushed."
  - line: 280
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck's claws sank into the loam, fingers curling around a fistful of bioluminescent roots as if they were the braids of his youngest daughter."
  - line: 281
    type: narration
    text: "Twelve names carved into his ribs—six sons, six daughters—each notch a vow to return before the white sky ate their stories."
  - line: 282
    type: narration
    text: "Now the sky had teeth, and his wife's last transmission had dissolved mid-sentence, her voice unraveling into static."
  - line: 284
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian warrior exhaled through slit nostrils, tasting the metallic tang of decision."
  - line: 285
    type: narration
    text: "His scales, usually the color of stormclouds, pulsed faintly with the Guild's new luminescence."
  - line: 286
    type: narration
    text: "The mission was done."
  - line: 287
    type: narration
    text: "The anchors were set."
  - line: 288
    type: narration
    text: "And yet—he flexed his claws—the white sky hadn't cracked."
  - line: 289
    type: narration
    text: "Not enough."
  - line: 291
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla's clay fingers paused mid-knead, sensing the shift in Oreck's posture."
  - line: 292
    type: narration
    text: "The golem didn't speak."
  - line: 293
    type: narration
    text: "He simply pushed a mound of luminous fungi toward the warrior, the offering glowing like a handful of stolen stars."
  - line: 295
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt watched from the perimeter line, his Dragon Mail humming with the weight of unsaid things."
  - line: 296
    type: narration
    text: "He knew that stillness—the moment before a man chooses between the living and the left-behind."
  - line: 297
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow twitched, her silver threads resonating with the Guild's network."
  - line: 298
    type: narration
    text: "She opened her mouth, but Oreck was already moving."
  - line: 300
    type: narration
    text: "The reptilian warrior crouched, pressing his forehead to the glowing earth."
  - line: 301
    type: narration
    text: "A hunter's prayer."
  - line: 302
    type: narration
    text: "A father's apology."
  - line: 303
    type: narration
    text: "Then he stood, shaking bioluminescent spores from his crest."
  - line: 304
    type: narration
    text: "\"The windless paths,\" he growled, echoing Kyh's earlier words."
  - line: 305
    type: narration
    text: "His claws flexed once—a gesture halfway between salute and severance—before he turned toward the trembling horizon."
  - line: 307
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn't stop him."
  - line: 308
    type: narration
    text: "Some roads only fit one set of footprints."
  - line: 310
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla grunted, patting the ground where Oreck had knelt."
  - line: 311
    type: narration
    text: "\"Good mortar,\" he muttered, though the clay between his fingers was wetter than before."
  - line: 312
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow stretched thin, her voice fraying at the edges."
  - line: 313
    type: narration
    text: "\"He'll die out there.\""
  - line: 315
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in Geralt's chest didn't waver."
  - line: 316
    type: narration
    text: "\"No,\" he said, watching Oreck's silhouette shrink against the white glare."
  - line: 317
    type: narration
    text: "\"He'll remind the sky what color it forgot.\""
  - line: 319
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere beyond the false horizon, twelve children waited."
  - line: 320
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere in the dissolving dark, a wife's unfinished sentence hung like a hook in the void."
  - line: 321
    type: narration
    text: "And Oreck—claws extended, crest raised—walked into the teeth of the storm with the only weapon the Queen couldn't erase: a story too heavy to unwrite."
  - line: 323
    type: narration
    text: "The ash clung to Geralt's thighs like a ghost's fingerprints—first one gust, then another, swirling the ember-flecked remnants of last night's fire directly into his lap."
  - line: 324
    type: narration
    text: "No wind had touched the camp."
  - line: 325
    type: narration
    text: "The air was still as a held breath."
  - line: 326
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow recoiled from the phenomenon, her edges flickering like a candle in a draft."
  - line: 327
    type: narration
    text: "\"Reality hiccups,\" Kulla muttered, kneading a fistful of clay into the ground as if to plug a leak."
  - line: 328
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt said nothing."
  - line: 329
    type: narration
    text: "He brushed the ash away, watching it dissolve before hitting the earth."
  - line: 330
    type: narration
    text: "Some farewells didn't need words."
  - line: 332
    type: narration
    text: "Morning arrived like a blade between the ribs—sudden, efficient, leaving no time to mourn."
  - line: 333
    type: narration
    text: "They packed in silence."
  - line: 334
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's canteen sloshed when he lifted it, half-empty from the night's ration."
  - line: 335
    type: narration
    text: "He set it down to adjust his gauntlet."
  - line: 336
    type: narration
    text: "When he picked it up again, the metal seared his palm with frost, moisture beading along the brim."
  - line: 337
    type: narration
    text: "Full."
  - line: 338
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's silver-threaded shadow pulsed once in alarm."
  - line: 339
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla sniffed the air."
  - line: 340
    type: narration
    text: "\"Time's cracked here,\" the golem observed, as casually as commenting on bad mortar."
  - line: 342
    type: narration
    text: "The fire was the last insult."
  - line: 343
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt doused it with their remaining water—a hissing protest of steam—only for flames to lick back to life the moment his back turned."
  - line: 344
    type: narration
    text: "Not embers."
  - line: 345
    type: narration
    text: "Not sparks."
  - line: 346
    type: narration
    text: "Full defiance, as if the universe had decided combustion was mandatory."
  - line: 347
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla stomped on it with one clay foot, grinding the coals into the damp earth."
  - line: 348
    type: narration
    text: "The fire gasped, died, then reignited in his footprint."
  - line: 350
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stopped mid-stride—and smiled."
  - line: 351
    type: narration
    text: "A slow, blade-sharp curve of lips that hadn't known warmth in decades."
  - line: 352
    type: narration
    text: "\"Alright,\" he murmured to the uncanny ash still clinging to his boots."
  - line: 353
    type: narration
    text: "\"Show yourself.\""
  - line: 355
    type: narration
    text: "The camp's southern edge answered first."
  - line: 356
    type: narration
    text: "A single blade of grass unspooled upward with impossible speed, its stem thickening, *remembering* itself—until Green Mika peeled free from the stalk like a butterfly emerging from chrysalis, verdant armor glinting in the false dawn."
  - line: 357
    type: narration
    text: "Behind her, the white sun flinched—just for a heartbeat—its sterile glow bleeding into buttery yellow."
  - line: 358
    type: narration
    text: "A single golden droplet swelled at its edge, fell, *splashed* against frozen earth—and Yellow Mika rose from the impact, her hair still dripping sunlight."
  - line: 360
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's canteen shattered against the ground."
  - line: 361
    type: narration
    text: "Not from impact—from expansion."
  - line: 362
    type: narration
    text: "The frozen water inside had grown teeth, claws, *purpose*, bursting its metal prison as Blue Mika coalesced from the spreading pool, liquid still cascading off her pauldrons in slow-motion droplets."
  - line: 363
    type: narration
    text: "To their left, the rebellious fire roared suddenly three meters high—not random, but *arched*, a gateway of writhing flame."
  - line: 364
    type: narration
    text: "Red Mika stepped through the infernal threshold unscathed, her armor drinking the fire like nectar."
  - line: 366
    type: narration
    text: "Then nothing."
  - line: 367
    type: narration
    text: "Five heartbeats of silence."
  - line: 368
    type: narration
    text: "Until the air six inches from Geralt's right elbow *bent*, twisted inward on itself—and Violet Mika materialized from the fold, her cloak still stitched with void-static."
  - line: 370
    type: narration
    text: "Together, they knelt."
  - line: 371
    type: narration
    text: "Not the stiff formality of vassals—this was collapse and reclamation, joints hitting earth like stones finding their rightful place in a landslide."
  - line: 372
    type: narration
    text: "When they spoke, the harmonics made Geralt's scorched Applicator whimper in recognition:"
  - line: 374
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Welcome back, Master.\""
  - line: 376
    type: narration
    text: "Not a greeting."
  - line: 377
    type: narration
    text: "A coronation."
  - line: 379
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow recoiled to the treeline, her silver threads snapping taut."
  - line: 380
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla paused mid-knead, his clay fingers suspending a lump of glowing fungi in disbelief."
  - line: 381
    type: narration
    text: "The Five Mikas didn't acknowledge them."
  - line: 382
    type: narration
    text: "Their focus was absolute—helmets tipped just enough to reveal the hollows where their eyes should be, each socket brimming with a different aspect of the spectrum Geralt had sacrificed to stabilize timelines."
  - line: 384
    type: narration
    text: "Green Mika's voice was photosynthesis given sound: \"You kept the roots alive.\""
  - line: 386
    type: narration
    text: "Yellow Mika's gauntlets flexed, molten gold dripping between her fingers: \"You carried the light when it burned.\""
  - line: 388
    type: narration
    text: "Blue Mika's chestplate still rippled with the memory of tidal forces: \"You held the shape of the vessel.\""
  - line: 390
    type: narration
    text: "Red Mika's breath smelled of kindling and old blood: \"You fed the flame when it starved.\""
  - line: 392
    type: narration
    text: "Violet Mika's cloak billowed without wind: \"You remembered the color they erased.\""
  - line: 394
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt exhaled."
  - line: 395
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in his chest didn't fade—it *recognized* itself."
  - line: 396
    type: narration
    text: "These weren't soldiers."
  - line: 397
    type: narration
    text: "They were his own scorch marks given sentience."
  - line: 398
    type: narration
    text: "\"Stand,\" he ordered softly."
  - line: 399
    type: narration
    text: "Five armored figures rose as one, their movements synchronized like fingers on a single hand."
  - line: 400
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, the false sun's cracks deepened another fraction."
  - line: 401
    type: narration
    text: "Some silences weren't empty—they were coiled."
  - line: 403
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla finally broke the stillness with a wet clay slap against his own thigh."
  - line: 404
    type: narration
    text: "\"Good mortar,\" he declared, as if that explained everything."
  - line: 405
    type: narration
    text: "Perhaps it did."
  - line: 407
    type: narration
    text: "The Five Mikas didn't dissolve—they *unfolded*."
  - line: 408
    type: narration
    text: "Green Mika's armor sprouted vines that sank into the earth; Yellow Mika stepped backward into her own lengthening shadow; Blue Mika's form cascaded apart like a breached dam."
  - line: 409
    type: narration
    text: "Only Violet Mika lingered long enough to press two fingers against Geralt's sternum—a touch colder than voidspace—before whispering coordinates that bypassed his ears entirely, etching themselves directly into the burnt pathways of his Applicator. *Echo Tower is empty.* The words tasted like oxidized copper and static. *Zypher moved beneath Tidecaller's Mountain."
  - line: 410
    type: narration
    text: "East becomes north when the sky bleeds white.*"
  - line: 412
    type: narration
    text: "Then she too was gone, her cloak's hem dissolving into the ozone-scented air where she'd stood."
  - line: 413
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt exhaled sharply—not at their departure, but at the *weight* of their message."
  - line: 414
    type: narration
    text: "Directions here weren't geography; they were living fractures in the Queen's porcelain reality. *North to go east.* He flexed his fingers, feeling the Guild's network hum in confirmation beneath his skin."
  - line: 415
    type: narration
    text: "Some paths only revealed themselves to those already broken enough to walk them."
  - line: 417
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow-form quivered at the treeline, her silver threads vibrating with stolen resonance."
  - line: 418
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Echo was her first lie,\" she murmured, more to herself than Geralt."
  - line: 419
    type: narration
    text: "\"A tower built to cast no shadow.\" Kulla grunted, slapping fresh clay onto a suddenly-unstable section of earth."
  - line: 420
    type: narration
    text: "\"Bad acoustics,\" he agreed, though his tone suggested he understood the deeper heresy—a place designed to swallow sound, memory, defiance."
  - line: 422
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt turned east—*true* east, the direction that had been forbidden when the white sky ate the old constellations."
  - line: 423
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in his chest pulsed once, an anchor finding its seabed."
  - line: 424
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere beneath Tidecaller's jagged peaks, Zypher was waiting."
  - line: 425
    type: narration
    text: "Not hiding. *Baiting.* The realization settled between Geralt's ribs with the certainty of a blade sliding home."
  - line: 426
    type: narration
    text: "This wasn't a rescue."
  - line: 427
    type: narration
    text: "It was a rendezvous between two scars on reality's skin."
  - line: 429
    type: narration
    text: "The ground trembled—not from seismic activity, but from the network adjusting its parameters."
  - line: 430
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla's clay fingers worked faster, patching cracks that wept luminescent spores."
  - line: 431
    type: narration
    text: "\"Going will hurt,\" the golem observed without looking up."
  - line: 432
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt didn't answer."
  - line: 433
    type: narration
    text: "He was already walking, each step compressing the distance between here and *east-that-was-north*, his boots leaving faint afterimages in the air."
  - line: 434
    type: narration
    text: "Behind him, Kyh's shadow stretched unnaturally long before snapping back into humanoid shape with a sound like tearing parchment."
  - line: 435
    type: narration
    text: "Some roads refused to be walked gently."
  - line: 437
    type: narration
    text: "They cut through Sundrift at dusk."
  - line: 438
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt counted seventeen empty market stalls where flower vendors once hawked moonblooms and fire-orchids."
  - line: 439
    type: narration
    text: "The fountain stood dry, its basin choked with dead leaves."
  - line: 440
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow stretched long across the cobbles, her silver threads probing the hollows between stones as if reading old footfalls."
  - line: 441
    type: narration
    text: "No familiar faces peered from shuttered windows."
  - line: 442
    type: narration
    text: "The silence tasted like a held breath—not abandonment, but evacuation."
  - line: 444
    type: narration
    text: "Falconridge was worse."
  - line: 445
    type: narration
    text: "The shack's roof had caved in under the weight of a fallen oak branch, its splintered wood gray with rot."
  - line: 446
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt knelt by the tombstone, brushing away moss with fingers that remembered the exact curve of Mika's hip beneath wool blankets."
  - line: 447
    type: narration
    text: "He laid a fistful of wild indigo—plucked from Sundrift's overgrown verges—against the granite."
  - line: 448
    type: narration
    text: "The petals trembled in a breeze that didn't touch the grass."
  - line: 450
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kyh
    text: "\"Time to go,\""
  - line: 452
    type: narration
    text: "Time to go,\" Kyh whispered."
  - line: 453
    type: narration
    text: "The indigo flowers withered mid-air, collapsing into ash before they hit the ground."
  - line: 454
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood, somewhere beyond, Zypher crouched beneath Tidecaller's Mountain, stitching defiance into the world's seams with a needle made of dragon teeth."
  - line: 456
    type: narration
    text: "—"
  - line: 458
    type: narration
    text: "The wall rose like a scar against the skyline—not the slapdash timber palisade Geralt remembered, but a seamless fusion of mortared stone and something darker, its surface glistening with the unnatural sheen of Queen-tech."
  - line: 459
    type: narration
    text: "Iron spikes crowned the ramparts at precise intervals, each one humming faintly in a frequency that made Geralt's molars ache."
  - line: 460
    type: narration
    text: "Sundrift's ghostly silence had been eerie, Falconridge's decay mournful—but Ironspire's new fortifications vibrated with a different energy entirely."
  - line: 461
    type: narration
    text: "Not memory."
  - line: 462
    type: narration
    text: "Amnesia enforced by steel."
  - line: 464
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"No admission without clearance,\""
  - line: 465
    type: narration
    text: "barked the sentry—though \"barked\" wasn't quite right. The voice came from a slit in the guard tower's obsidian face, but the words had the rehearsed cadence of a recording. Kyh's shadow twitched, her silver threads probing the ground for unseen tripwires. Kulla sniffed the air and frowned. \"Bad mortar,\" he muttered, scratching at his clay arms. \"Smells like... pressed bones.\""
  - line: 467
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stepped forward, deliberately keeping his hands visible."
  - line: 468
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in his chest didn't waver, but his Applicator sparked—a warning."
  - line: 469
    type: narration
    text: "Something about the wall's geometry was wrong."
  - line: 470
    type: narration
    text: "Its height should have cast shadows across the approach, yet the ground remained uniformly lit, as if the structure existed in a separate pocket of spacetime."
  - line: 471
    type: narration
    text: "\"We're Guild,\" he said, watching the sentry slit for any flicker of recognition."
  - line: 472
    type: narration
    text: "\"Network anchors.\""
  - line: 474
    type: narration
    text: "A pause."
  - line: 475
    type: narration
    text: "Then, with mechanical precision: \"No Guild presence registered in Ironspire Sector.\" The slit snapped shut."
  - line: 476
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's breath hitched—not at the rejection, but at what she'd glimpsed in that fractional opening."
  - line: 477
    type: narration
    text: "\"The guard,\" she whispered."
  - line: 478
    type: narration
    text: "\"His eyes were—\""
  - line: 480
    type: narration
    text: "A klaxon drowned her words."
  - line: 481
    type: narration
    text: "From the ramparts, hexagonal panels slid aside, revealing arrays of crystalline barrels that swiveled in unison."
  - line: 482
    type: narration
    text: "Not ballistae."
  - line: 483
    type: narration
    text: "Not even cannons."
  - line: 484
    type: narration
    text: "These were Spire-tech—miniaturized versions of the asteroid facility's applicators, their apertures already glowing the particular white-blue of akashic erasure."
  - line: 486
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla grabbed Geralt's elbow with surprising urgency."
  - line: 487
    type: narration
    text: "His clay fingers left dents in the Dragon Mail."
  - line: 488
    type: narration
    text: "\"Run,\" he growled—not in fear, but in the tone of a mason warning about structural collapse."
  - line: 489
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, the ground where they'd stood moments earlier *unfolded*, reality itself peeling back to reveal the hungry void beneath the Queen's new world order."
  - line: 491
    type: narration
    text: "The wall hadn't been built to keep people out."
  - line: 492
    type: narration
    text: "It had been constructed to erase whatever didn't fit inside."
  - line: 494
    type: narration
    text: "The fissure wasn't a crack—it was a wound."
  - line: 495
    type: narration
    text: "Not in the rock, but in the Queen's perfect geometry."
  - line: 496
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's fingers found purchase where there should have been none, his gauntlets scraping against mineral veins that pulsed faintly with old magic."
  - line: 497
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere above, Kyh's shadow-form oozed through a hairline fracture that should have been impassable, her silver threads vibrating with stolen resonance."
  - line: 498
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla climbed last, his clay fingers reshaping themselves to grip surfaces that crumbled under his touch like stale bread."
  - line: 500
    type: narration
    text: "They emerged into air that smelled of lightning-struck granite and something darker—ozone with teeth."
  - line: 501
    type: narration
    text: "The ground here wasn't ground at all, but the corpse of an older mountain, its bones ground to powder and reshaped into the Queen's parody of order."
  - line: 502
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's boots sank slightly, the earth remembering itself just long enough to bear their weight before reverting to sterile dust."
  - line: 503
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, the fissure sealed with a sound like a ribcage collapsing."
  - line: 505
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh materialized fully first, her edges frayed from squeezing through realities."
  - line: 506
    type: narration
    text: "\"The network doesn't recognize this place,\" she murmured, staring at her palms where silver threads should have glowed."
  - line: 507
    type: narration
    text: "Instead, they lay dormant—not severed, but muted."
  - line: 508
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla knelt immediately, plunging both hands wrist-deep into the ashen soil."
  - line: 509
    type: narration
    text: "His clay fingers moved like a surgeon's, probing for fractures."
  - line: 510
    type: narration
    text: "When he withdrew them, the tips were smoking slightly."
  - line: 511
    type: narration
    text: "\"Buried harmonics,\" he grunted."
  - line: 512
    type: narration
    text: "\"Old ones.\""
  - line: 514
    type: narration
    text: "The rear gate groaned like a dying beast, its iron hinges shearing apart with unnatural precision."
  - line: 515
    type: narration
    text: "Five horsemen emerged—not in a charge, but in a synchronized glide, their mounts' hooves barely disturbing the dust."
  - line: 516
    type: narration
    text: "Their armor wasn't steel; it was something grown, plates overlapping like insect carapace, each segment pulsing with the same white-blue glow as the wall's cannons."
  - line: 517
    type: narration
    text: "The lead rider's visor slid open with a wet sound, revealing a face that was half-human, half something pressed into human shape."
  - line: 518
    type: narration
    text: "His tongue flicked out—forked, glistening—as he spoke in a voice that came from his chest rather than his throat: \"Lay down your stolen tools.\""
  - line: 520
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla's clay fingers stopped kneading abruptly."
  - line: 521
    type: narration
    text: "\"Not horses,\" he muttered."
  - line: 522
    type: narration
    text: "The creatures' flanks shimmered where muscle should be, their bodies distending slightly with each breath as if barely containing something larger."
  - line: 523
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow recoiled into a tighter knot behind Geralt."
  - line: 524
    type: narration
    text: "\"They're wearing the riders,\" she breathed."
  - line: 525
    type: narration
    text: "\"Not riding them.\""
  - line: 527
    type: narration
    text: "The lead horseman's gauntlet twitched—a gesture that should have drawn a sword."
  - line: 528
    type: narration
    text: "Instead, the air between them rippled, and Geralt's Applicator screamed inside his skull."
  - line: 529
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in his chest flared hot for the first time in months as he recognized the sensation: localized causality failure."
  - line: 530
    type: narration
    text: "These weren't enforcers."
  - line: 531
    type: narration
    text: "They were walking Spire fragments, their very presence unraveling the possibility of defiance."
  - line: 533
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt exhaled through his teeth."
  - line: 534
    type: narration
    text: "A single drop of water fell from his canteen—the one he'd stabilized during Kaelen's training."
  - line: 535
    type: narration
    text: "It hung in the air, perfectly inelastic, as the Five Mikas had taught him."
  - line: 536
    type: narration
    text: "The lead horseman's head cocked at an impossible angle, his neck vertebrae clicking like beads on a string."
  - line: 537
    type: narration
    text: "\"You persist,\" he observed, as if commenting on a mildly interesting fungus."
  - line: 538
    type: narration
    text: "\"How mortal.\""
  - line: 540
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla lunged first—not at the riders, but at the ground between them."
  - line: 541
    type: narration
    text: "His clay hands plunged elbow-deep into the earth with a sound like tearing meat."
  - line: 542
    type: narration
    text: "The horsemen's mounts shrieked, their forelegs suddenly mired in what should have been solid ground."
  - line: 543
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow lashed out like a whip, her silver threads slicing through the second rider's reins—except they weren't reins at all, but pulsing umbilical cords."
  - line: 544
    type: narration
    text: "Something dark and viscous spurted from the severed connection."
  - line: 546
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt moved last."
  - line: 547
    type: narration
    text: "Not because he hesitated, but because his body had become the anchor point for a different kind of physics now."
  - line: 548
    type: narration
    text: "When his fist connected with the lead horseman's chest, the impact didn't send the rider flying—it sent reality itself recoiling in a concentric shockwave."
  - line: 549
    type: narration
    text: "The carapace armor cracked like eggshell, revealing writhing Spire-code beneath."
  - line: 550
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in Geralt's chest held firm."
  - line: 551
    type: narration
    text: "This wasn't a battle."
  - line: 552
    type: narration
    text: "It was punctuation."
  - line: 554
    type: narration
    text: "From the ruptured armor, a familiar voice emerged—not the rider's, but the Applicator's, twisted and scorched from its last encounter with the Spire: *The whip-hand can choose to drop the whip.*"
  - line: 556
    type: narration
    text: "The remaining horsemen froze."
  - line: 557
    type: narration
    text: "Not in surrender."
  - line: 558
    type: narration
    text: "In recognition."
  - line: 559
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt bared his teeth."
  - line: 560
    type: narration
    text: "Behind him, the inelastic water drop finally hit the ground."
  - line: 562
    type: narration
    text: "Some silences were louder than war cries."
  - line: 564
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt turned and kept walking."
  - line: 565
    type: narration
    text: "The crunch of boots on gravel was louder than the shrieks behind him—not because the sounds weren't horrific, but because his numbness had become a tuning fork, resonating only with the path ahead."
  - line: 566
    type: narration
    text: "The lead horseman's gurgling protest died mid-syllable, replaced by a wet *thock*—the sound of a helmet hitting dirt after its contents had been evacuated through the eye sockets."
  - line: 567
    type: narration
    text: "He didn't need to look."
  - line: 568
    type: narration
    text: "He knew the rhythm of Mika's work by now."
  - line: 570
    type: narration
    text: "Blue Mika flickered into existence beside a rearing mount, her form liquid and precise."
  - line: 571
    type: narration
    text: "The horse-thing's neck snapped sideways at an angle that defied vertebrate biology just as she dissolved into mist."
  - line: 572
    type: narration
    text: "Yellow Mika materialized inside another rider's chestplate, her molten gauntlets flexing once before vanishing—leaving the carapace armor glowing cherry-red from the inside out."
  - line: 573
    type: narration
    text: "A half-second later, the rider slumped forward, his ribcage collapsed into charcoal."
  - line: 574
    type: narration
    text: "Red Mika didn't bother with subtlety; she stepped *through* the third horseman like a candle flame through parchment, her passage igniting his spinal column into a torch that burned without fuel or smoke."
  - line: 576
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt counted their footfalls instead of screams."
  - line: 577
    type: narration
    text: "Violet Mika's absence was the loudest—until reality itself hiccuped, and the last two riders simply ceased mid-stride, their outlines fraying like poorly rendered ink sketches."
  - line: 578
    type: narration
    text: "Only then did Violet Mika condense from the empty air beside Geralt, her cloak still rippling with afterimages of erased spacetime."
  - line: 579
    type: narration
    text: "\"Cleaner this way,\" she murmured, though her voice came from everywhere and nowhere, a harmonic pressed between seconds."
  - line: 581
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, the horsemen's remains collapsed into constituent elements—bone ash, spent Spire-code, the sourceless smell of burnt copper."
  - line: 582
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla stomped on a still-twitching umbilical cord with the solemnity of a mason laying bricks."
  - line: 583
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh's shadow pooled around the wreckage, her threads harvesting stray frequencies before they could destabilize further."
  - line: 585
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt adjusted his cuff."
  - line: 586
    type: narration
    text: "Some battles weren't fought; they were autopsied."
  - line: 587
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness in his chest yawned wider, grateful."
  - line: 589
    type: narration
    text: "End of chapter 55"

